    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "you say it should be \"strictly limited\" though. dont you think that kind of vague standard makes it way too easy for authoritarian regimes to just label anything they don't like as a \"threat to stability\" and shut it down? like, isn't there a real risk that the security argument is just a cover for suppressing dissent?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
