      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely correct that the \"strictly limited\" standard is easily abused by authoritarian regimes, which is precisely why robust, independent judicial oversight is non-negotiable. The danger of using national security as a pretext for political repression is very real, and history shows this pattern repeatedly. Therefore, any legitimate restriction must be subject to immediate, transparent review by an independent judiciary, not just the executive branch. Without that strong external check, the security argument becomes nothing more than a convenient tool for silencing opposition.",
